<header class="hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">GDSL · Public API example</p>
  <h1>Compute with GDSL<br>in your own app.</h1>
  <p class="lede">Mix two streams, then accumulate. A few JavaScript calls build a typed PVGraph; the built-in engine checks it and runs it on the CPU or WebGPU.</p>
  <div class="hero-tags"><span>Local modules</span><span>One shared dataflow language</span><span>No SPARQL required</span></div>
</header>

<section class="pipeline" aria-label="The computation">
  <div><span>01 · MAP</span><strong>Amplify A</strong><code>a × gain</code></div>
  <div><span>02 · ZIP</span><strong>Mix in B</strong><code>amplified + b</code></div>
  <div><span>03 · SCAN</span><strong>Accumulate</strong><code>inclusive prefix sum</code></div>
</section>

<div class="workspace">
  <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="inputs-title">
    <div class="panel-title"><h2 id="inputs-title">1. Make it yours</h2><span class="tag">UNSIGNED 32-BIT WORDS</span></div>
    <div class="sample-controls">
      <label for="sample-size">Sample size
        <select id="sample-size"><option value="8">8 · inspect each word</option><option value="2048">2,048 · parallel scan</option><option value="4096">4,096 · larger sample</option></select>
      </label>
      <button id="load-sample" type="button" class="secondary">Load sample</button>
    </div>
    <label for="input-a">Input A <span>JSON array</span></label>
    <textarea id="input-a" rows="4" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="off" autocorrect="off">[2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19]</textarea>
    <label for="input-b">Input B <span>JSON array · same length</span></label>
    <textarea id="input-b" rows="4" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="off" autocorrect="off">[1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6, 5]</textarea>
    <div class="input-row">
      <label for="gain">Gain for A<input id="gain" type="number" min="0" max="4294967295" step="1" value="3"></label>
      <label for="execution-mode">Execution mode
        <select id="execution-mode"><option value="auto">Automatic · try GPU, allow CPU</option><option value="cpu">CPU · reference evaluator</option><option value="gpu">Required GPU · refuse if unavailable</option></select>
      </label>
    </div>
    <p class="small">Arithmetic wraps modulo 2<sup>32</sup>. This editor accepts 0–4,096 words per input. Empty inputs are valid. The engine checks the PVGraph and input shapes.</p>
    <button id="run-example" class="primary" type="button">Run computation</button>
    <p id="run-status" class="status" role="status">Ready. The engine loads when you run.</p>
    <details>
      <summary>Local runtime and GPU threshold</summary>
      <label for="package-url">Local package directory<input id="package-url" type="text" value="{{ '/npm/factoidal/' | url }}" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off"></label>
      <label for="assets-url">Wasm assets directory <span>optional</span><input id="assets-url" type="text" placeholder="Default: l4-assets/ beside browser.js" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off"></label>
      <label for="minimum-words">Minimum words for an automatic GPU attempt<input id="minimum-words" type="number" min="0" max="4194240" step="1" value="0"></label>
      <p class="small">The demo uses <code>minWords: 0</code> to exercise WebGPU with small inputs. The API default is 1,024. This threshold is a diagnostic choice, not a speed claim. Required GPU mode ignores it.</p>
      <p class="small">The package directory must be on this page's HTTP origin. It supplies <code>gdsl.mjs</code>, <code>browser.js</code> and the matching Wasm. Reload the page to change an already loaded runtime.</p>
      <p id="runtime-status" class="status">No runtime loaded. No CDN modules are used.</p>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section class="panel results" aria-labelledby="results-title">
