<section class="panel integration" id="use-in-app" aria-labelledby="integration-title">
  <div class="panel-title"><h2 id="integration-title">3. Use it in another app</h2><span class="tag">PUBLIC MODULES ONLY</span></div>
  <p>The code below uses your current inputs and settings. Put the repository's <code>npm/factoidal/</code> directory at <code>vendor/factoidal/</code> beside your app, including its installed <code>l4-assets/</code>. Serve that directory from localhost or HTTPS. The downloaded HTML is a complete independent app.</p>
  <div class="actions"><button id="copy-code" type="button" class="secondary">Copy JavaScript module</button><button id="download-app" type="button" class="secondary">Download standalone HTML</button></div>
  <p id="code-status" class="status" role="status">Imports use your local vendor/factoidal directory.</p>
  <pre id="integration-code" tabindex="0" aria-label="Complete JavaScript integration example">The example code appears when JavaScript loads.</pre>
  <details>
    <summary>File layout and package imports</summary>
    <ul><li><code>gdsl-example.html</code> — the downloaded app.</li><li><code>vendor/factoidal/gdsl.mjs</code> and <code>browser.js</code> — public entry points.</li><li><code>vendor/factoidal/lib/</code> — package support modules.</li><li><code>vendor/factoidal/l4-assets/</code> — the matching installed engine.</li></ul>
    <p>For example, run <code>python3 -m http.server 8080</code> in your app directory, then open <code>http://localhost:8080/gdsl-example.html</code>.</p>
    <p>The package declares the corresponding <code>@factoidal/core/gdsl</code> and <code>@factoidal/core/browser</code> imports for bundlers and package consumers. Use the local checkout for this example; npm publication is a separate release step.</p>
    <p><a href="https://github.com/danbri/factoidal-core/blob/main/docs/web/hub/gdsl-app/README.md">Setup and reusable recipe</a> · <a href="https://github.com/danbri/factoidal-core/blob/main/npm/factoidal/gdsl.d.ts">TypeScript API</a></p>
  </details>
</section>

<section class="panel assurance" id="evidence" aria-labelledby="assurance-title">
  <h2 id="assurance-title">What is checked?</h2>
  <p>Lean/Wasm constructs, admits and plans the same PVGraph document that this app uses. The GPU path runs the emitted plan and, with <code>verifyWithLean: true</code>, compares every output word with the reference evaluator. The app contains no second implementation of those operators.</p>
  <p>The pure model's theorems and this per-run comparison have distinct roles. Compilation, the host interface, WGSL execution, drivers and devices remain execution boundaries; a matching run does not prove hardware correctness or a performance advantage.</p>
  <p><a href="https://github.com/danbri/factoidal-core/blob/main/docs/specs/gdsl-0.2.md">GDSL specification and operator profile</a> · <a href="{{ '/web/hub/gssl/' | url }}">PVGraph workbench</a> · <a href="{{ '/web/hub/gpu-sparql/' | url }}">SPARQL integration</a> · <a href="https://github.com/danbri/factoidal-core/issues/741">App integration record</a></p>
</section>
<noscript>This example needs JavaScript and the local Wasm engine. WebGPU also needs a supported browser in a secure context.</noscript>
